\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Ride on, ride on in majesty!
\par Hark! All the tribes Hosanna! cry;
\par O Saviour meek, pursue Thy road
\par With palms and scattered garments strowed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Ride on, ride on in majesty!
\par In lowly pomp ride on to die;
\par O Christ, Thy triumphs now begin
\par O 'er captive death and conquered sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Ride on, ride on in majesty!
\par The winged squadrons of the sky
\par Look down with sad and wondering eyes
\par To see the approaching sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Ride on, ride on in majesty!
\par Thy last and fiercest strife is nigh;
\par The Father on His sapphire throne
\par Expects His own anointed Son.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Ride on, ride on in majesty!
\par In lowly pomp ride on to die;
\par Bow Thy meek head to mortal pain,
\par Then take, O God, Thy power, and reign.\f1 
\par 
\par }

